    "text": {
     "en": "We use grams for small weights and kilograms for bigger ones. 1 kilogram is 1000 grams.\nWe use millilitres for small amounts of liquid and litres for larger ones. 1 litre is 1000 millilitres.\nHalf a kilogram is 500 grams. A quarter of a kilogram is 250 grams.\nChoose the right unit: a pencil in grams, a bag of rice in kilograms, a spoon of medicine in millilitres, a bucket in litres."
